# issue: none
# notes: The roll-back leg of the #601 heal: the arm put is misdirected to `__recovery/dstm-<opid>.json` and the confirm put then fails, so the mutation surfaces the injected error and the foreign-named sidecar stays Armed with no visible commit.
# notes: The reopen lists the foreign file, rolls the intent back, and deletes the sidecar at the uri it was listed from; the write after the reopen succeeds and the rolled-back row is absent. The sibling cases `issue_601_*` cover the roll-forward leg (mutation published, reopen finalizes).
# notes: Two seams before one step name distinct seams (RFC 0066); the failing confirm put is `mutation_sidecar_confirm_put_failure_rolls_back.gqt` with the misdirect added.
# notes: Red on the unfixed engine (`recovery.rs` of fe9eb339, 2026-09-16): step 3 refused with RecoveryRequired "pending Mutation recovery operation blocks writes on branch 'main'", the same barrier the `issue_601_*` cases were red on; the reopen had deleted the canonical name and left the foreign file.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine-dst
    storage: in-memory-object-store
    seeds: [0]

--- schema
node Person {
    name: String @key
}

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"name":"alice"}}

--- seam
at: recovery.sidecar_write
occurrence: 1
action: misdirect
scope: next_step

--- seam
at: mutation.sidecar_confirm_put
occurrence: 1
action: fail
scope: next_step

--- mutate
query add_row() {
    insert Person { name: "bob" }
}

--- expect error: injected failpoint triggered: mutation.sidecar_confirm_put

--- restart

--- mutate
query add_row_after_reopen() {
    insert Person { name: "carol" }
}

--- expect affected: nodes=1 edges=0

--- query
query rows_after_reopen() {
    match { $p: Person }
    return { $p.name }
}

--- expect unordered
{"p.name":"alice"}
{"p.name":"carol"}

--- expect shape
p.name: String
